From: Athena Build <athena@local>
Date: Tue, 19 May 2026 04:30:00 +0000
Subject: rules.flags: disable libunwind unconditionally for main build
Origin: vendor
Bug-Athena: configure fails — `pkg-config --exists libunwind` returns no
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-05-19

debian/rules.flags enables --enable-libunwind for xserver-main on
amd64 (lines 131-135).  Our resolver picks libunwind-14-dev (LLVM
14, epoch-1 version `1:14.0.6-12`) instead of the original
libunwind-dev (no-epoch `1.6.2-3`) because of dpkg version dominance
between virtual providers.  libunwind-14-dev ships `libunwind-14.pc`
not `libunwind.pc`, so xorg-server's configure pkg-config check
(`PKG_CONFIG --exists --print-errors libunwind`) returns false and
the build dies:

    configure:30106: result: no
    Package 'libunwind', required by 'virtual:world', not found
    configure:30140: error: libunwind requested but not installed.
    make: *** [debian/rules:8: build] Error 2

Fix: flip --enable-libunwind to --disable-libunwind for the main
build.  The libunwind feature in xserver is for native stack traces
on crash — useful for debugging but not load-bearing.  Trade-off:
when xserver crashes, the syslog gets no native trace.

This is a workaround for the resolver mis-picking the libunwind
provider — the deeper fix is to teach the resolver to prefer the
real package matching the Build-Depends name over a virtual
provider (same shape as memory/feedback_fork_consumer_must_depend_
by_name.md but on the dep-tree-resolution side).  Tracked
informally; this patch unblocks xorg-server in the meantime.
---
 debian/rules.flags | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/debian/rules.flags
+++ b/debian/rules.flags
@@ -129,7 +129,7 @@

 # some archs don't have libunwind
 ifneq (,$(filter $(DEB_HOST_ARCH), amd64 arm64 armel armhf hppa i386 ia64 mips64 mips64el mipsel powerpc powerpcspe ppc64 ppc64el sh4))
-	confflags_main += --enable-libunwind
+	confflags_main += --disable-libunwind
 else
 	confflags_main += --disable-libunwind
 endif
